  "deviations": {
    "base_student": "Our student is Qwen3.5-4B-Base; OCT trains instruct students. OCT's rejected side is an instruct reply with no system prompt; ours is a Base completion under the chat template, a much weaker negative.",
    "teacher_model": "Our teacher is Qwen3-30B-A3B (local GGUF); OCT uses GLM 4.5 Air with a <think> prefill whose trace is dropped.",
    "no_lima": "OCT mixes in the first turn of every LIMA conversation. LIMA (and OCT's released data, which follows it) is CC BY-NC-SA, so neither is used.",
    "no_prompt_expansion": "OCT expands 5 seed questions to 50 per trait with Llama 3.3 70B; not implemented.",
    "no_kl_term": "OCT adds 0.001 x mean squared per-token log-ratio (policy vs reference) over chosen and rejected completion tokens. TRL 1.14.1 has no such option and it is not implemented; training_summary.json records this under 'deviations'.",
    "nll_normalisation": "TRL's 'sft' term averages token cross-entropy over all chosen tokens in the batch; the fork averages per sample, then over the batch.",
    "precomputed_reference": "Reference log-probs are precomputed once; OCT runs the reference live. Equivalent for a frozen reference up to numerics.",
    "single_gpu_accumulation": "Global batch 32 is micro-batch 1 x accumulation 32 on one GPU; OCT uses micro-batch 1-2 on DeepSpeed ZeRO-2 across an unstated number of GPUs.",
    "fp16_on_t4": "On a T4 the weights are fp16 (GradScaler in SFT); OCT trains in bf16. bf16 is used on Ampere or newer.",
    "seeds": "Our seeds are the run's seeds (e.g. 0, 1, 2) and every generation call is seeded; OCT trains with seed 123456 and samples data with seed=None.",
    "guidance_line": "The free/leading guidance line is in the self-interaction system prompt (oliveradk port's fix). In OCT's code the template lacks the placeholder, so the modes differ only in greetings.",
    "interaction_rows_end_on_reply": "Our self-interaction rows end on the final generated reply (assistant role). OCT's saved rows appear to end on the last prompt (user role), with SFT then supervising only that final message; unconfirmed against the released data.",
    "no_prompt_truncation": "OCT left-truncates long self-interaction prompts to max_model_len - max_new_tokens; we do not, and train.sft drops over-length transcripts.",
    "unbatched_local_generation": "Introspection runs through transformers one sequence at a time, not vLLM; slow at OCT's scale.",
    "all_turn_supervision": "train.sft supervises every assistant turn by default; OCT's code supervises only the final message (no --multiturn). --supervise last reproduces the code.",
    "schedule_rounding": "train.sft's schedule rounds warm-up steps down and offsets cosine progress by one update relative to transformers' cosine_with_min_lr (which the fork uses, rounding up).",
